What this licence covers, and what it does not

The text above covers this repository's own files: the adapter, the core's
own display, sound and platform layers and the test runners under waterbox/,
the test program generator under waterbox/tests/, the build files, and the
documents.

The patches under patches/ are changes to ZEsarUX and are under ZEsarUX's
terms, the GNU General Public License version 3 or later.

It does not cover what the repository builds from. The emulator is ZEsarUX,
by Cesar Hernandez Bano and its contributors
(https://github.com/chernandezba/zesarux), under the GNU General Public
License version 3 or later, at the commit pinned in extern/zesarux (the
release ZEsarUX 13.0). ZEsarUX includes modules by other authors under their
own terms; its file src/LICENSES_info lists them and its folder
src/licenses holds their texts. One of them, PlayTZX, is left out of the
core because ZEsarUX's note says its licence is unknown.

The program in the built package, zesarux.chimeraCore, is therefore under
the GNU General Public License version 3 or later.
waterbox/package-licenses.json lists every component with its licence and
where its source is, and the built package carries their licence texts.

No ROM, firmware, SD card image or game is in this repository or in the
built package. The ZX Spectrum Next's boot ROM (tbblue_loader.rom), the ZX
Spectrum 48K ROM (48.rom) and the SD card image with the Next's system on
it are supplied by the user. ZEsarUX's repository, which is this
repository's submodule, does contain copies of all three; the tests read
them from there, and nothing of them is copied into this repository.
